{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-22-Dec-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 22, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Pipes A and B can fill an empty cistern in 65 minutes and 26 minutes, respectively. Both Pipe A and Pipe B are opened together. After how much time should Pipe B be turned off so that the empty cistern is completely filled in a total of 30 minutes?", "options": [{"text": "20 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "15 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "10 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "14 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "fill-empty", "key_answer": "14 minutes"}, {"n": 2, "text": "Ramesh bought an article for ₹5,000 and sold it to Suresh at a profit of 20%. Suresh then sold it further at a loss of 10%. For how much did Suresh sell the article?", "options": [{"text": "₹5,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,800", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "₹5,400"}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "54.54%", "added": false}, {"text": "37.27%", "added": false}, {"text": "42.27%", "added": false}, {"text": "27.27%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": "27.27%"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A train passes a station platform in 60 seconds and a man standing on the platform in 40 seconds. If the speed of the train is 63 km/hr, calculate the length of the platform.", "options": [{"text": "300 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "350 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "550 metres", "added": false}, {"text": "400 metres", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "350 metres"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The mode of the observations 21, 29, 35, 24, 25, 33, 24, 23, 26, 28, 35, 27, 20, 35 and 20 is:4288", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "29", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "35"}, {"n": 6, "text": "Simplify: [(9x + 4y)2 − (9x − 4y)2​] ÷ 24x", "options": [{"text": "16x", "added": false}, {"text": "8x", "added": false}, {"text": "6y", "added": false}, {"text": "12xy", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "16"}, {"n": 7, "text": "An item is sold for ₹6,500 after two successive discounts of 35% and 20%. What is the marked price (in ₹) of the item?", "options": [{"text": "12,674", "added": false}, {"text": "12,500", "added": false}, {"text": "12,435", "added": false}, {"text": "12,560", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "12,500"}, {"n": 8, "text": "The monthly incomes of two friends Mukund and Sachin are in the ratio 5 : 9 respectively and each of them saves ₹45,000 every month. If the ratio of their monthly expenditure is 1 : 3, then find the monthly income of Mukund (in ₹).", "options": [{"text": "74,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,05,000", "added": false}, {"text": "75,000", "added": false}, {"text": "76,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "75,000"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The price of a branded pen is ₹180 and that of a pencil is ₹3.50. If the total price of x branded pens and y pencils is ₹935 and x + y = 15, then what is the value of (x2 + y2)?", "options": [{"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "164", "added": false}, {"text": "205", "added": false}, {"text": "181", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": "125"}, {"n": 10, "text": "Simplify: [(9x + 4y)2 − (9x − 4y)2​] ÷ 24x", "options": [{"text": "16x", "added": false}, {"text": "8x", "added": false}, {"text": "6y", "added": false}, {"text": "12xy", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": "6y"}, {"n": 11, "text": "In quadrilateral PQRS, the bisectors of ∠ R and ∠ S meet at the point T (inside the quadrilateral) and ∠ STR = 36°. If the ratio of ∠ P to ∠ Q is 3 : 5, then what is the difference between the measures of ∠ Q and ∠ P?", "options": [{"text": "18°", "added": false}, {"text": "21°", "added": false}, {"text": "25°", "added": false}, {"text": "22°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "18°"}, {"n": 12, "text": "A, B and C can do a piece of work in 2, 4 and 4 days, respectively. How long (in days) will they take to do thrice the same work, working together?", "options": [{"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 13, "text": "Find the single discount (approximately) equal to three consecutive discounts of 6%, 5% and 11%.", "options": [{"text": "21.73%", "added": false}, {"text": "20.52%", "added": false}, {"text": "23.23%", "added": false}, {"text": "21.86%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": "20.52%"}, {"n": 14, "text": "₹5,575 is divided among X, Y and Z in such a way that if ₹85, ₹65 and ₹61 is deducted from their respective shares, they have money in the ratio 5:11:20. Find the difference between the original shares of Y and Z.", "options": [{"text": "₹1,191", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,241", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,337", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,491", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": "₹1,337"}, {"n": 15, "text": "Find the ratio between the fourth proportional of 4, 8 and 19 to the mean proportional of 9 and 4.", "options": [{"text": "19 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "22 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "16 : 9", "added": false}, {"text": "19 : 4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "19 : 3"}, {"n": 16, "text": "Find the smallest number which when increased by 10 is completely divisible by 12, 15, 18 and 20.", "options": [{"text": "170", "added": false}, {"text": "200", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}, {"text": "190", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "170"}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "26 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "80 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "13 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "169 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "other", "key_answer": "26 cm"}, {"n": 18, "text": "A camp has provisions for 20 pupils for 12 days. In how many days will the same provisions be used up, if the strength of the camp is increased to 80 pupils?", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "direct-inverse-variation", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 19, "text": "The amount on a sum of ₹4,800 at 15% per annum compound interest, compounded annually, in 2 years will be:", "options": [{"text": "₹7,194", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,348", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,717", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,836", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": "₹6,348"}, {"n": 20, "text": "The distance between points A and B is 933 km. Namit travels from A to B at a speed of 70 km/hr and returns at a speed of 111 km/hr. Calculate Namit’s average speed for the entire journey (rounded off to two decimal places).", "options": [{"text": "85.86 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "81.26 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "88.58 km/hr", "added": false}, {"text": "94.58 km/hr", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": "85.86 km/hr"}, {"n": 21, "text": "The product of the present ages of Ram and Lalith is 216 years, and their age ratio is 6 : 1. Find the difference in their ages.", "options": [{"text": "18 years", "added": false}, {"text": "36 years", "added": false}, {"text": "30 years", "added": false}, {"text": "24 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "ratio-of-ages", "key_answer": "30 years"}, {"n": 22, "text": "The expenditure of Sudha is 200% more than her savings. If her expenditure decreases by 10% and savings increase by 34%, then by what percentage does her income increase?", "options": [{"text": "1%", "added": false}, {"text": "3%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}, {"text": "6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "1%"}]}